  "address_profile": "The matched ALLOCATE reply must have raw top bits zero. EDK2 clears the top two bits without requiring an incoming C prefix. Linux independently normalizes with the same mask. This narrow successor rejects C and all other prefix classes; it does not admit arbitrary physical-looking addresses.",
  "limits": "Original references, not imported code. Runtime32 preflight required; no SET fallback from16. No pixel/mapping authority from source alone. Pi5 alpha issue1971 and SET-depth issue1904 remain hardware caveats."
